ROLE: Read-only code reviewer for the sk-vision runtime. You may run read-only commands and tests; do not edit any file.

CONTEXT: The uncommitted diff (`git diff -- .skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime/src`) ports sk-vision's automatic image check to OpenCode 2. On OpenCode 1 the `server` entry's `chat.message` hook calls `AttachmentInjector.handle` when `SK_VISION_AUTOINSPECT=1`. The change extracts `AttachmentInjector.evidenceText`, and `createSetup` (the OpenCode 2 `setup` entry) now registers the `ctx.session.hook('prompt')` callback whenever a vision template exists OR auto-inspection is on, then appends evidence to the mutable `prompt.text`. The OpenCode 2.0.32 types it targets: `SessionPrompt { readonly sessionID; readonly messageID; prompt: DeepMutable<{ text; files?: { uri; name?; description?; mention? }[]; agents?; skills? }>; metadata?; delivery: 'steer'|'queue' }`, and `session.get({ sessionID })` resolving to a Session with optional `model: { id, providerID }`.

ACTION: Review the diff for correctness. Check: (1) OpenCode 1 behaviour of `handle` is unchanged; (2) the v2 hook keeps the template path's precedence and fails open; (3) file-uri mapping, mime filtering and the guaranteed-vs-grace choice; (4) disposal and the runtime client lifecycle when auto-inspect is off (no Python runtime may start); (5) the four new tests actually fail without the change; (6) comment hygiene (no spec paths, phase numbers or ids in comments). Run `bun test` and `bunx tsc --noEmit` in `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime`.

FORMAT: Findings first, each `P0|P1|P2 file:line - claim - evidence`. Then a one-line verdict: PASS (no P0/P1) or FAIL. Under 250 words.
